% =============================================================================
% IEEEtran.bst control entry. Not a reference -- it sets style options.
%
% The only option that matters here is CTLdash_repeated_names. By default
% IEEEtran.bst replaces the author list with an em-dash run ("------, ...")
% whenever consecutive entries share the same authors, which affected three
% references: the two Ribeiro papers following the ds003690 dataset entry, and
% the ARAUS corrigendum following the ARAUS dataset paper. IEEE's own citation
% export spells the names out ("K. Ooi et al., ..."), three dashed entries in a
% row is hard to read, and a reference beginning with a dash is easy to mistake
% for a broken entry -- which is exactly what happened during review of this
% file. Turned off.
%
% Reaching it requires \bstctlcite{IEEEtranBSTCTL:soundml} before the first
% real citation. IEEEtran.cls defines \bstctlcite; the supplement uses the
% article class and defines it in its own preamble.
@IEEEtranBSTCTL{IEEEtranBSTCTL:soundml,
  CTLdash_repeated_names = "no"
}

