% Mostly generated by scripts/58_build_references.py from Crossref, but NOT
% purely generated -- read this before re-running that script.
%
% Crossref deposits are lossy in three ways this file has had to repair, all
% found by resolving every DOI against a second source (Semantic Scholar,
% PubMed, DataCite):
%
%   1. ACM strips the subtitle after the colon, so "ESC: Dataset for
%      Environmental Sound Classification" arrives as "ESC" and "XGBoost: A
%      Scalable Tree Boosting System" as "XGBoost". The generator's expected
%      titles had been degraded to match the stubs, so its own reverse check
%      could no longer catch this.
%   2. Author arrays are truncated at 15 with no "and others", and some
%      publishers (Frontiers) deposit only the first author. unsrtnat prints
%      whatever it is given as if it were complete.
%   3. Some deposits carry the online-first year rather than the issue year.
%
% unsrtnat applies sentence case to titles, so every acronym and proper noun is
% brace-protected. Without the braces the reference list prints "Esc",
% "Xgboost", "Clap", "Biraffe2", "Pmemo".
%
% HAND-MAINTAINED, absent from the generator's WANTED list -- re-running
% scripts/58_build_references.py will delete these unless it is updated first:
