% preprint" rather than referred to vaguely: a reader who wants to see what
% changed can fetch it, and a reviewer who finds it independently is not left
% to wonder whether we knew.
% The identifier goes in `howpublished`, not only in `eprint`. IEEEtran.bst
% ignores eprint/archivePrefix/primaryClass unless CTLuse_url is on, so the
% first version of this entry rendered as "... modelling," 2026." -- a
% citation to a preprint with no way to find the preprint, which defeats the
% reason for citing it. `eprint` is kept for anyone using a style that reads it.
@misc{zhang2026preprint,
